---@class cloudflare.rate_limits.CreateRateLimitRequest
---@field zone_id string Defines an identifier.
---@field action cloudflare.rate_limits.CreateRequestAction The action to perform when the threshold of matched traffic within the configured period is exceeded.
---@field match cloudflare.rate_limits.CreateRequestMatch Determines which traffic the rate limit counts towards the threshold.
---@field period number The time in seconds (an integer value) to count matching traffic. If the count exceeds the configured threshold within this period, Cloudflare will perform the configured action.
---@field threshold number The threshold that will trigger the configured mitigation action. Configure this value along with the `period` property to establish a threshold per period.

---@class cloudflare.rate_limits.CreateRateLimitResponse

---@class cloudflare.rate_limits.CreateRequestAction
---@field mode? cloudflare.rate_limits.CreateRequestActionMode|string The action to perform.
---@field response? cloudflare.rate_limits.CreateRequestActionResponse A custom content type and reponse to return when the threshold is exceeded. The custom response configured in this object will override the custom error for the zone. This object is optional. Notes: If you omit this object, Cloudflare will use the default HTML error page. If "mode" is "challenge", "managed_challenge", or "js_challenge", Cloudflare will use the zone challenge pages and you should not provide the "response" object.
---@field timeout? number The time in seconds during which Cloudflare will perform the mitigation action. Must be an integer value greater than or equal to the period. Notes: If "mode" is "challenge", "managed_challenge", or "js_challenge", Cloudflare will use the zone's Challenge Passage time and you should not provide this value.

---@alias cloudflare.rate_limits.CreateRequestActionMode "simulate"|"ban"|"challenge"|"js_challenge"|"managed_challenge"

